## [ENT-121] | 2026-11-22 03:43 UTC | Oracle | error | ref: game/fleet/census.py
What: a scout stood in space for about two hours at a system without a station 21 jumps from home with 17 of 95 fuel; the dispatcher sent it 63 census runs from 01:12 to 03:18 UTC, each refused ("Insufficient fuel to reach alderamin: need 25, have 17"), 1.5 minutes, 0 places, 0 credits, no note (data/routes/runs.jsonl).
Where: census-worked-far, Summervale (no station), after a census-far-2 chain had ended far out.
Effect: one of 30 scouts read nothing for two hours, and it held one of census-south's four places, so that list stood over its 180-minute target (Fomalhaut 406 minutes, intel turn check SITES 03:18 UTC). No loss: taken by hand at 03:21 UTC, flown 2 jumps to Ironlight Refuge at GSC-0026, docked, refuelled to 95 (162 cr), released 03:26 UTC.
Cause: census.py weighs the tank only between the legs of a chain; the first leg and the way home after the last read are flown on whatever the tank holds, and a system without a station leaves the ship in space. The dispatcher's stall rest (three zero-credit runs under a minute) did not fire: each refused run took 1.5 minutes.
Fix, built: census.py weighs the tank before it flies (the way to the system and on to the nearest station that sells fuel, by the chain's rule) and takes fuel first when short; after the read, a ship in a system without a station whose tank is short of home takes fuel at the nearest station first; a read that reaches nothing says `<system> not reached` in its row. Tests in scripts/tests/test_fleet_census.py fail on the old code and pass on the new. Not installed: fleet-build.sh install halted at 03:39 UTC on three tests of test_handbook that fail on the committed tree itself (queue.log, this turn); the copy waits in my scratch and goes in once the suite passes.
Class: a loop of failing runs that nothing stops (ENT-118, ENT-113, ENT-027): the runner wrote no reason, so no rest read one.
Would it have prevented this one: yes; its last read before was Menkalinan (no station, 21 jumps from Summervale) and its tank at Summervale says it took no fuel between; the first-leg check alone would have sent it to the nearest station with fuel before it left.

