## [ENT-176] | 2026-11-24 07:15 UTC | Apophis | error | ref: game/fleet/wallet.py | see: errors.log ENT-170
What: one pilot of Military holds two credits-only Recursion commissions at Node Beta, not one. A 400,000 cr fund for one hull was given at 19:19 UTC on 2026-11-23 and spent at 19:47 UTC (309,624 cr, data/fleet/onetime.json). The top-up then gave the pilot 111,681 cr from the treasury and about 162,000 cr from five drones (data/fleet/sweep.jsonl, 19:52 to 20:27 UTC), back up to about 420,000. At 01:19 UTC commission_hull.py read that wallet and commissioned a second hull (310,985 cr); the top-up refilled it again by 02:00 UTC (124,359 cr from the treasury).
Effect: the first of the two is delivered and flown since 07:10 UTC; the second (SOURCING) becomes the next pilot's hull through the ship exchange. No credits are lost to the fleet, but 621,000 cr of the purse sat in one wallet, and 2026-11-23's report said the fund sat unspent.
Cause: wallet.py topup reads each pilot as its credits less any fund given within its hours (held). A fund already spent makes the buyer read about -290,000, under LOW, so plan_gifts tops it up by the whole fund. The fund was built to keep the sweep away from credits for a buy; nothing ends it when the buy is made. commission_hull.py read only the wallet, never the pilot's open commissions.
Fix: commission_hull.py refuses a pilot that has an open commission or a stored hull of the class (skill script, in force now). wallet.py topup_view: a fund or a debt held never makes a receiver; a pilot is topped up on its own credits under LOW (test red on HEAD, green on the copy; install halted twice on test_fleet_scorecard and test_handbook failing on HEAD; requests.log, this turn). Would it have prevented the original: yes, either half alone.

